<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4760" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">azȳmus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">azymon</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Prud. Apoth.
		421</span></i>), a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄζυμος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>unleavened</i> (very freq. in Vulg.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">azymi panes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Exod. 12, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">ib.
				Jud. 6, 21</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">panis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 133</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lagana azyma,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Lev. 2, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">ib. 1 Par. 23, 29</span></i>; and so <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">azȳma</span></b> , ōrum,
			n., <i><span class="en">Vulg. Exod. 12, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">ib. Lev. 8,
				2 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Esp., of the Jewish feast of unleavened bread: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dies festus azymorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Luc. 22, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dies azymorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					Act. 12, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">20, 6</span></i>; also <i>absol.</i>: Erat
			pascha et azyma (Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">`͂Ην τὸ πάσχα καὶ τὰ
				ἄζυμα</span>), <i><span class="en">ib. Marc. 14,
			1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>unleavened</i>, i.
			e. <i>morally uncorrupted</i>, <i>pure</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sicut estis azymi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1
					Cor. 5, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in azymis sinceritatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. ib. 5, 8</span></i>
			. 
			
			</div>
